message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite the paper."
title: "Positional Information Causally Constrains Background Shortcut Reliance in Vision Transformers"
abstract: >-
  Scaling the positional signal of eight identically trained Vision Transformer
  checkpoints shows that attenuating positional information monotonically raises
  background-shortcut reliance on ImageNet-9, that the encoding scheme is irrelevant,
  and that the effect is specific to spatial information loss rather than generic
  degradation.
